  "question": {
    "text": "The volume&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>V</mi></math> of a given mass of monoatomic gas changes with temperature&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi></math> according to the relation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>K</mi><msup><mi>T</mi><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></msup></math>. The workdone when temperature changes by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>90</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>&nbsp;will be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mi>R</mi></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>&nbsp;is<br />[<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math>&nbsp;universal gas constant ]"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "60",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>We know that work done is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>W</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>&#8747;</mo><mi>P</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>V</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mi>R</mi><mi>T</mi></mrow><mi>V</mi></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>W</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>&#8747;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mi>R</mi><mi>T</mi></mrow><mi>V</mi></mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>v</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>3</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>K</mi><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>4</mn></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>W</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>&#8747;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mi>R</mi><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#183;</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>v</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>5</mn></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo></math> from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>4</mn></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mi>K</mi><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mi>d</mi><mi>T</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>W</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mo>&#8747;</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msubsup><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mi>R</mi><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>K</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>T</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>W</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mi>n</mi><mi>R</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>6</mn></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>90</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>7</mn></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>W</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mi>n</mi><mi>R</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>90</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>W</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>60</mn><mi>n</mi><mi>R</mi></math></p><p>Assuming <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;mole of gas</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p>So <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>W</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>60</mn><mi>R</mi></math></p>"
  }
